  "full_response": "Sure, I'd be happy to provide a comprehensive comparison of the major cloud providers: Amazon Web Services (AWS), Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud Platform (GCP). Below is an overview of 20 key service categories with the pros cons for each provider.\n\n### 1. Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS)\n\n- **Amazon Web Services (AWS)**\n  - **Pros:** EBS, EC2,3, RDS, Lambda. Best for global reach.\n  - **Cons:** Complex and steep learning curve, Lambda service billing can be unpredictable.\n\n- **Microsoft Azure**\n  - **Pros:** VMs, App Service, Cosmos DB, Azure Functions. Good integration with Microsoft products.\n  - **Cons:** Pricing can be complex. Some services (like Cosmos DB) are not delivered as soon as advertised.\n\n- **Google Cloud Platform (GCP)**\n  - **Pros:** Compute Engine, Cloud Functions, Firestore, Bigtable. Simple pricing model; features often come for free.\n  - **Cons:** Limited geographical reach compared to AWS; can be expensive.\n\n### 2. Platform as a Service (PaaS)\n\n- **Amazon Web Services (AWS)**\n  - **Pros:** Elastic Beanstalk, Lightsail. Designed to scale, industry-leading SDKs.\n  - **Cons:** AWS Elastic Beanstalk is less customizable compared to private deployment.\n\n- **Microsoft Azure**\n  - **Pros:** Azure App Service, Azure Functions, Cognitive Services. Strong CI/CD integration with Azure DevOps.\n  - **Cons:** Platform can be resource-intensive; pricing might be high for small scale projects.\n\n- **Google Cloud Platform (GCP)**\n  - **Pros:** App Engine, Cloud Run, Cloud Datastore, Cloud SQL. Simple pricing, can be faster deployment.\n  - **Cons:** Limited customizations; can be unconventional compared to AWS/Azure.\n\n### 3. Serverless Computing\n\n- **Amazon Web Services (AWS)**\n  - **Pros:** Lambda, Step Functions API Gateway. Flexible and powerful.\n  - **Cons:** Cold starts can increase latency, billing is opaque sometimes.\n\n- **Microsoft Azure**\n  - **Pros:** Azure Functions, Logic Apps, SignalR. Good for building everything from radios to databases.\n  - **Cons:** Can be tricky to optimize for performance; similar issues of starts.\n\n- **Google Cloud Platform (GCP)**\n  - **Pros:** Cloud Functions, Cloud Pub/Sub, Cloud Run. Simple pricing,",
